#X text 17 68 [snake~ split] splits a multichannel into 2 output signals (mono or multichannel). The left outlets contains the first 'n' channels of the input. If 'n' is 0 (default) \, the left output is a mono signal of zeroes. Similarly \, if 'n' equals the amount of input channels \, the right outlet will be a mono signal of zeroes. The index is set via the argument \, the 'index' message or a float into the right inlet. An index change updates the DSP graph., f 86;
